  "prompt_before_text_permission": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset: one 4:3 landscape painting for The Burnt Book Sanskrit learning story. Request 1536 x 1152 native output or the closest supported native 4:3 resolution. Refined Indian watercolor with restrained gouache on warm ivory paper; organic detail, quiet ochre, sage, dusty terracotta, muted indigo. Warm, gentle, evocative storytelling, consistent character design.\nCanonical scene brief: The Vetāla seated on a tree root, folded like a long grey umbrella, eyes closed, telling a tale; Dādī and Śuka sitting before him; the faint backwards-walking spirit crouched beside; at the dark edge of the trees Lubdhaka leaning in to listen, the lantern low.\nCharacter appearances:\nyou: Always seen from behind or at a distance, face never detailed, so every learner can be the hero: a young person in a simple ochre kurta with a cloth shoulder bag.\ndadi: A warm, sharp-eyed grandmother in her seventies, silver hair in a low bun, round spectacles, a cream cotton sari with a thin maroon border and a grey shawl; carries a cloth-bound notebook.\nshuka: A bright green rose-ringed parrot with a red beak and a faint pink and black neck ring, a little scruffy, very expressive eyes; usually on your shoulder or Dādī's.\nvetala: A long, thin, ash-grey spirit hanging upside down from a śiṃśapā branch by its ankles, arms folded across its chest, bright amused eyes, a shawl of mist trailing downwards; strange, never frightening.\natitaka: A pale, almost see-through spirit whose edges fade like old ink, walking backwards and leaving a trail of fading footprints.\nlubdhaka: A tall man in an expensive dark coat over a kurta, rings on his fingers, a leather satchel, usually half in shadow; never monstrous.\nPhone-first composition: clear compact narrative grouping, essential faces, hands and objects comfortably inside all edges. Show the complete scene without border. No collage or multi-panel layout.\nMANDATORY TEXT OVERRIDE: this card authorizes NO writing in the painting. Where the scene brief or character description mentions letters, a register, script, writing, numbers, sacred symbols or letter-shaped objects, show the corresponding physical door, pillar, book, leaf, crown or cord WITHOUT any letters or letterlike marks. Use purely floral carvings and completely blank smooth manuscript surfaces. Teaching letters remain separate live app text. No typography, numerals, Om signs, invented script, explanatory marks, sound lines, watermark or labels anywhere.",
